The evidence points to one fault. The ts-route-service pod restarted during the window, and its server spans stop for about 90 seconds. I'm reporting it as `pod_failure`, since the pod briefly stops and then recovers. The findings:

```json
{
  "root_causes": [
    {
      "service": "ts-route-service",
      "fault_kind": "pod_failure",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "kind": "trace",
          "sql": "WITH s AS (SELECT time FROM abnormal_traces WHERE service_name='ts-route-service' AND attr_span_kind='Server' ORDER BY time), g AS (SELECT time, LAG(time) OVER (ORDER BY time) AS prev FROM s) SELECT prev, time, date_diff('second', prev, time) AS gap_s FROM g WHERE date_diff('second', prev, time) > 20 ORDER BY gap_s DESC LIMIT 5",
          "claim": "ts-route-service server spans stop for about 90 seconds (roughly 15:22:07 to 15:23:36) and then resume."
        },
        {
          "kind": "log",
          "sql": "SELECT time, attr_k8s_pod_name, level, attr_log_template FROM abnormal_logs WHERE service_name='ts-route-service' AND (attr_log_template LIKE 'Started RouteApplication%' OR attr_log_template LIKE 'Starting RouteApplication%') ORDER BY time",
          "claim": "ts-route-service application restarted during the incident, starting at about 15:23:08 and finishing startup at 15:23:36."
        },
        {
          "kind": "trace",
          "sql": "SELECT date_trunc('minute', time) AS m, sum(CASE WHEN attr_http_response_status_code=502 THEN 1 ELSE 0 END) AS err502, count(*) AS total FROM abnormal_traces WHERE service_name='loadgenerator' AND span_name LIKE '%routeservice/routes%' GROUP BY 1 ORDER BY 1",
          "claim": "Loadgenerator GET /routeservice/routes returns 502 in 15:22 and 15:23, matching the route-service gap; 200s otherwise."
        },
        {
          "kind": "trace",
          "sql": "WITH bad AS (SELECT trace_id FROM abnormal_traces WHERE service_name='loadgenerator' AND attr_http_response_status_code=502) SELECT t.service_name, t.span_name, t.attr_span_kind, t.attr_http_response_status_code, count(*) c FROM abnormal_traces t JOIN bad USING(trace_id) GROUP BY ALL ORDER BY c DESC",
          "claim": "The 502 requests never reach ts-route-service: their traces contain only the ts-ui-dashboard server span, with no downstream calls."
        },
        {
          "kind": "metric",
          "sql": "SELECT date_trunc('minute', time) AS m, sum(value) AS tcp_flag_events FROM abnormal_metrics_sum WHERE metric='hubble_tcp_flags_total' AND attr_source LIKE '%ui-dashboard%' AND attr_destination LIKE '%route-service%' GROUP BY 1 ORDER BY 1",
          "claim": "TCP flag events on the ui-dashboard to route-service connection rise about 16x during the outage window versus normal."
        }
      ]
    }
  ],
  "propagation": [
    {
      "from": "ts-route-service",
      "to": "ts-ui-dashboard",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "kind": "trace",
          "sql": "SELECT date_trunc('minute', time) AS m, sum(CASE WHEN attr_http_response_status_code=502 THEN 1 ELSE 0 END) AS err502, count(*) AS total FROM abnormal_traces WHERE service_name='loadgenerator' AND span_name LIKE '%routeservice/routes%' GROUP BY 1 ORDER BY 1",
          "claim": "User-facing GET /api/v1/routeservice/routes requests fail with 502 through ts-ui-dashboard while ts-route-service is down."
        }
      ]
    }
  ]
}
```

